    <exercise number="55" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>[T] A certain bacterium grows in culture in a circular region. The radius of the circle, measured in centimeters, is given by $$r(t) = 6 - \left\lbrack {5/\left( {t^{2} + 1} \right)} \right\rbrack,$$ where t is time measured in hours since a circle of a 1-cm radius of the bacterium was put into the culture.</paragraph>
        <list type="ordered">
          <item>Express the area of the bacteria as a function of time.</item>
          <item>Find the exact and approximate area of the bacterial culture in 3 hours.</item>
          <item>Express the circumference of the bacteria as a function of time.</item>
          <item>Find the exact and approximate circumference of the bacteria in 3 hours.</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>a. $$A(t)=A(r(t))=\pi \cdot (6-5t2+1)2A(t)=A(r(t))=\pi \cdot (6-5t2+1)2$$ b. Exact: $$121\pi 4;121\pi 4;$$ approximately 95 cm2 c. $$C(t)=C(r(t))=2\pi (6-5t2+1)C(t)=C(r(t))=2\pi (6-5t2+1)$$ d. Exact: $$11\pi ;11\pi ;$$ approximately 35 cm</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
